Chapter 7: Afferent Feedback for Embodiment

For the wings to be incorporated into the body schema, sensory feedback must be congruent and low‑latency:

· Lift magnitude → pressure belt (pneumatic) around thorax.
· Wing position → 8×8 vibrotactile grid on the back encoding stroke plane and feathering.
· Efficiency → sonification of lift‑to‑drag ratio.
· Vestibular state → artificial horizon in AR glasses.

Target end‑to‑end latency: < 50 ms for tactile, < 100 ms for auditory/visual.

