Chapter 8: Experimental Validation Roadmap

8.1 Minimum Viable Experiment (Year 1)

Goal: Falsify H1 with minimal hardware.

· Setup: VR headset, IMU harness, non‑invasive EEG cap. User controls a 2‑DOF lift vector (sagittal plane) via two‑class motor imagery (e.g., imagined left‑hand vs. right‑hand movement mapped to forward/up lift). The copilot stabilises the remaining 6 wing DOFs.
· Independent variable: BCI ITR, varied by session number (training).
· Dependent variable: Achieved lift tracking error, vestibular disturbance norm.
· Prediction: The trade‑off curve between ITR and tracking error will saturate; below 60 bits/min, error exceeds the dynamic stall margin, confirming the rate‑distortion bound.

8.2 Full‑Scale Experiments

· Experiment 2: Wind‑tunnel validation of UBET with physical wing prototype.
· Experiment 3: Shared autonomy benchmark in VR with 4‑parameter user control, comparing full‑human, shared, and full‑autonomy conditions.

