Appendix F – Control Barrier Function Construction and Robustness (Theorems 5.1, 5.2)

F.1 Safe Set and CBF Condition
The vestibular safe set is

\mathcal{C} = \{ \mathbf{x} \mid h(\mathbf{x}) \ge 0 \}, \qquad h(\mathbf{x}) = \min_i (a_{i,\max} - |\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w|),

where  a_{i,\max}  are the allowable linear and angular acceleration limits. Because  h  is not differentiable everywhere (absolute value), we smooth it with a continuous approximation or treat each constraint separately:  h_i(\mathbf{x}) = a_{i,\max}^2 - (\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w)^2  so long as  \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w  is differentiable. The control input appears through  \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w  (velocity), so the barrier condition is

L_{\mathbf{f}} h_i + L_{\mathbf{g}} h_i \, \mathbf{u} + \lambda h_i \ge 0,

where  \mathbf{u} = \ddot{\mathbf{q}}_w . Because  \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w  is part of the state and  \ddot{\mathbf{q}}_w  is the control, the Lie derivative  L_{\mathbf{g}} h_i = -2 (\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w) \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} . Feasibility of the QP is guaranteed because the copilot can always reduce flapping amplitude (choose  \mathbf{u}  to drive  \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w  to zero).

F.2 Robustness to Harness Uncertainty (Proposition 5.2)
The true vestibular Jacobian is  \tilde{\mathbf{J}}_{\mathrm{vest}} = \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest}} + \Delta\mathbf{J} , with  \|\Delta\mathbf{J}\| \le \epsilon . The true vestibular acceleration is  \tilde{a}_i = \tilde{\mathbf{J}}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w . The nominal CBF uses the model  \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest}} . To guarantee  \tilde{a}_i^2 \le a_{i,\max}^2 , we enforce a tightened constraint:

h_i^{\mathrm{rob}}(\mathbf{x}) = a_{i,\max}^2 - (\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w)^2 - \epsilon \|\dot{\mathbf{q}}_w\| (2 a_{i,\max} + \epsilon \|\dot{\mathbf{q}}_w\|) \ge 0 .

Then for any  \Delta\mathbf{J} ,

|(\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} + \Delta\mathbf{J}_i) \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w| \le |\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{vest},i} \dot{\mathbf{q}}_w| + \epsilon \|\dot{\mathbf{q}}_w\| \le a_{i,\max},

provided the tightened condition holds. This yields a robust CBF that can be incorporated into the MPC.

